        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Augustus</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">63 BCE – 14 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">23 September 63 BCE, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, at a family property on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatine-hill">Palatine Hill</a>; son of Gaius Octavius, of an equestrian branch of the gens Octavia, and Atia, niece of Julius Caesar</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">19 August 14 CE, at Nola, of natural causes at the age of 75; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassius-dio">Cassius Dio</a> claimed that his wife Livia poisoned him, which many historians dismiss</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a> from 43 BCE; triumvir from 43 BCE; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princeps">princeps</a> and first Roman emperor, with the title augustus, from 27 BCE to 14 CE; pontifex maximus from 12 BCE; pater patriae from 2 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">founding the principate; victory at Actium over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Cleopatra; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pax-romana">Pax Romana</a>; the annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and wide conquests; the Res Gestae Divi Augusti; reform of taxation and the army; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/praetorian-guard">Praetorian Guard</a>; rebuilding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in marble</span></div>
