    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Named heir by his great-uncle Julius Caesar, Octavian used Caesar's money, name and veterans to win the civil wars that followed the assassination of 44 BCE.</li><li>From 27 BCE he kept the forms of the Republic while holding the army, half the provinces and a growing set of powers, a system known as the principate.</li><li>His reign brought conquests, a standing army, tax reform and a long peace, but it began with proscriptions and executions, and writers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> to Ronald <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syme">Syme</a> have judged it an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/autocracy">autocracy</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Roman month of Sextilis was renamed August after him in 8 BCE; he chose it because it was the month of his first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">consulship</a> and of several of his victories.</p></aside>
    </section>

